WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:05.320
Tell me, Brother, what kind of
ability do you think Level 6 will be?

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.820
That's something I don't know, either, mm-mm.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.410
Huh? Even though you're
telling me I should become one?

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.160
Hirumi, you know about the Level 5s, right?

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.040
Hmm, you mean like the standalone third-ranked,

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
who's as powerful as a battle cruiser?

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:23.250
Or the first-ranked, who you
couldn't even hurt with a nuke?

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.380
They all sound like urban legends.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:31.510
That's because the stage you're
seeing them at, at least, looks blurred.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:34.350
And a monster who's at Level 6? Mm-hmm...

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:39.230
Even higher than the first-ranked,
who won't die no matter what.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:40.350
Hirumi?

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.270
Today, I was introduced to my hope--

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:51.240
the dream of my brother and me.
The hope that would lead to Level 6--

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.740
the necromancer Esther.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.160
Wow. Now we're using
necromancers? Or -cy?

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:08.050
Oh yeah? So now we're going in that direction?

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:10.510
Hirumi, I think that's enough for today.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.350
I was picturing someone in
a musty, old-fashioned lab coat.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.810
Hey, come on, go home already.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.850
I'm musty?

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.400
You speak Japanese!

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.360
I was requested to come here.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.820
But what is this place?

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:34.240
Oh, these are your forerunners, mm-hmm.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:39.330
Relics of when our research hit a dead end,
and we looked for outside hints.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:43.580
We brought in some OOPArts
and extracts from cryptids,

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.380
but now, we've brought in a person.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:49.420
What happened with that
legendary metal, orichalcum, again?

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.670
I forget what number we were on.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:54.220
That was our third sample.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:58.300
Although, it was just a
simple alloy of iron and brass.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.760
That's my forerunner?

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.980
I am not made of metal.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:07.190
Oh, mm-hmm, nor are you
a carboxylic acid ester.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:09.320
Brother, she won't get that.

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:13.030
Conversely, I'd like to ask,
how am I supposed to see eye-to-eye

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:15.530
with someone who doesn't
even know about polyester?

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.330
I apologize. Brother likes
to flaunt his useless knowledge,

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:22.080
and can't maintain his composure
unless he has the upper hand.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.870
He's a real pain in the butt.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:27.920
Okay, fine, just get on out of here, Hirumi.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:32.050
What I'm saying is,
we'd like you to work with us, Esther.

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:34.220
O-On what?

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.480
Are you okay?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.690
To our brother-and-sister dream--

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:58.700
of achieving the world's first Level 6.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:06.250
Just to confirm, I use necromancy.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:09.080
This is a systemic technique
to load and control a pseudo-soul

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.170
into a dead body that
was prepared ahead of time.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:16.260
For that purpose, I even brought
my precious Si-xiong charms.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.380
Qiongqi...

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:18.590
...Hundun...

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:19.760
...Taotie...

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.560
...and Taowu.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.850
You're free to believe in those
powers if you want to, mm-hmm.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:30.190
Then what do you call <i>that</i>?

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:33.900
I can't work those machines.
What is it you're after?

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:39.780
I'm researching the hypothesis that
abilities reside within the body, mm-hmm.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:49.330
Specifically, I'm using injections
to numb the cerebellum, the brainstem,

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:52.540
and other internal organs, one at a time.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:55.800
If they can still use their
abilities in that state, they pass;

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.050
if they can't, it raises a red flag.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.010
And...?

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:02.640
I can't exactly conduct experiments
with the spinal cord or the heart stopped

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.600
when they're directly
related to life support, can I?

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:08.560
So I needed something else
that can step in to do so.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.310
And now, thanks to this over-the-top front end,

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:15.280
I'm starting to lose sight of my prototype.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.400
All right, let's call it a day.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.650
That's not what I meant.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.200
Hmm?

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.740
I'm asking how knowing where an ability resides

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:27.580
relates to being able to elevate
a person to this "Level 6" thing?!

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:31.420
Hmm, it doesn't really relate at all, mm-mm.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:41.130
Why exactly did they call me in?

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.640
For whom?

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.220
Here!

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.930
To do what?

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.390
Ah, jeez!

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:57.070
Why did you bounce it there?!

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:04.070
Oh, no! Don't tell me she's...

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:09.700
Esther!!

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:12.750
Slow down, Esther! What are you doing?!

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:16.460
Are you the legendary "Undresstress"?!

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:19.880
I was just going to go
for a dip to calm my mind.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:23.930
This is not the sort of place to do that!

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:25.640
Huh?

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:26.640
Come on, with me!

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:29.470
H-Hold on...

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.810
I knew it. She's not the legendary
"Undresstress" after all.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:33.940
Oh, Yo...

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:38.190
Man, what a letdown. Let's go, let's go.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:44.490
If you want to go bathing,
you can knock yourself out here.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:48.450
I have a change of clothes for you.
I'll leave them in the dressing room.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.760
It's a distressing country
if I can't even go bathing.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:09.930
You look pretty good in that outfit.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:13.730
What do you think of my coordinating skills?
The size is perfect, too, right?

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:18.190
Those clothes are a present for you.
Take good care of them.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:21.690
Also, you'd usually get arrested
for doing that outside.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:26.110
But then, if anything happened,
Brother would get it swept under the rug.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.620
Is that right?

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:33.250
You should be grateful.
He seems to really appreciate you, Esther.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:41.090
She doesn't look very good at this.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:43.300
This is my training for the day.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:50.470
What you like and what you're good
at aren't always necessarily the same.

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:55.020
I understand that, too.

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:05.190
Well, <i>you're</i> not Hirumi.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.570
She said she didn't have anything today.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:12.910
I sent her home. I checked her vitals,
and her waveforms are unsteady.

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:15.580
The fatigue must be
catching up to her, mm-hmm.

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:17.920
Hey, Hishigata, that may be so,

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:21.170
but we can't proceed
with the research without a subject.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:26.050
It's more unusual that we gave Hirumi
a regular account in the first place.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:30.850
I know we had other subjects.
Someone somewhere messed them up, though.

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:33.850
Should we recruit additional volunteers?

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:38.560
Name-brand bags and fur coats.
I'm not sure if they're photo-worthy or not,

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:42.190
but are you telling me that we found
more than enough teenage girls

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.780
who have gotten themselves into debt
and will do whatever they're told?

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:47.490
So, what do we do?

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:52.330
Search me. Maybe scout out some habitual
shoplifters this time? Mm-hmm.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:54.290
Aw, I was afraid of that.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:58.830
Just because they were a little broken,
we shouldn't have let them go.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:01.130
The research equipment
tuning has been finished,

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:03.040
and Esther is here as our safety.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:06.880
We were finally going to produce some results.

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.090
You sure are calm, Esther.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:13.300
I am a necromancer,
and I'm used to a certain amount of tragedy.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:16.470
Hmm, well, I guess
that's not really too irregular.

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:19.440
It's just that they may
never use their abilities again,

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:23.110
or they might not ever escape
the dream world, is all, mm-hmm.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:27.860
That reminds me, we talked about
where the abilities reside, remember?

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:29.530
In the course of that research,

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:34.160
a separate bit of
fascinating data came up, mm-hmm.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:37.080
We started discovering
that during the experiment,

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:40.670
the output of the subject's ability
was much greater than it usually was.

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:42.920
At first we thought that
by shutting down a specific organ,

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:47.000
it was like unplugging a stopper,
but we were wrong.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:50.340
The bigger the equipment
that served as the subjects' bodies was,

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:54.220
the more they were able
to draw out their ability, mm-hmm.

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:56.100
Making the equipment larger

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:58.600
to let the subjects feel like
their bodies had gotten bigger

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:00.480
elevated their abilities.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.560
But when we make the equipment
bigger to elevate their abilities,

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.780
if we make them <i>too</i> big,
it destroys the girls' sense of self, mm-hmm.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:11.450
The reasons are unclear.
Maybe it's diluting them--

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:15.870
having too small a mind inside too big a body.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:16.950
Mind?

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:19.040
The mind and the soul are things,

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:22.250
as a scientist, I have to turn
a blind eye to dealing with,

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:25.130
but you <i>do</i> deal with these things, right?

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:26.500
Well...

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.880
If we can just keep the
dilution of the mind under control,

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:33.430
we'll be able to hook up external
expansion equipment as large as we like.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:37.050
Theoretically, there will be
no limit on our room for growth.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:42.060
In other words, the time will come
when anyone can reach Level 6 easily.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.480
You mean you've been doing
these experiments on Hirumi, too?

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:46.480
I made it look like we were,

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:50.570
but then I fed her a
separate diversionary program.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:53.490
You have no idea how much
my nerves fray each time,

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:56.990
making sure she doesn't become aware of it.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:02.580
Hirumi is too fixated on Level 6, mm-hmm.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:07.540
Even though, before long, the time will
come when anyone can easily achieve it.

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:15.640
What? You look like you're going to say

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:19.350
that eating so much after
exercising makes it pointless.

00:10:19.350 --> 00:10:24.020
No, just questioning where you're
going to fit all of that inside your body.

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:29.360
Well, it's not like I'm working out
so I can lose weight.

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:32.280
Besides, at this point...

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:36.740
Unless you want to eat it together?
Esther, you're like family to me.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:40.330
Here, once we finish it,
we'll go back to the lab.

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:42.540
You're our secret weapon, right?

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:46.120
Brother says you use a power
they've never seen before.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.750
I'm looking forward to it.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:52.550
Secret weapon, huh? I just hope that's true.

00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:54.010
Hmm?

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:57.760
I've been thinking a lot about
what kind of power necromancy

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:02.180
and the Rosenthal style
of techniques really are.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:06.480
Even after being requested to come here,
I still haven't found an answer.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:12.320
Hmm, so what you're saying is, you want
to be useful to someone, right, Esther?

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:13.400
Huh?

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:15.030
I'm the same way.

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:20.240
I want to help Brother out.
That's why my goal is to reach Level 6.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.330
That's great for you, Hirumi. But as for me...

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:25.450
Okay, you can help <i>me</i> out!

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:26.370
Huh?

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.670
If I ever need anything, you can do it for me!

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:32.550
When you say "do it," what does that mean?

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:34.800
Promise me, Esther!

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:35.760
Promise you?

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:37.170
Yep.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:40.970
A promise, made between me and Esther.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.140
Just you and me.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:45.350
Huh? Okay...

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:56.110
See? That's what you get
for trying to eat that giant thing.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:57.490
No way, no way!

00:11:57.490 --> 00:12:00.490
I am not letting you take part
in experiments with the equipment

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:01.870
until I give the say-so!

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:04.120
--But...
--I won't have you talking back to me, either!

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:05.950
Hishigata, Hirumi is doing this for you--

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:10.790
You keep quiet. Mm-hmm.
This is a matter between brother and sister.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:15.090
Now that Esther is here, we can clear
all the problems we've had so far, right?

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:17.800
You think I'd rely on a safety device
whose logic I don't understand

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:20.430
and give the go signal
to a full-blown experiment

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:23.140
that could put my sister's life at risk?

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:27.480
We haven't even seen this
"necromancy" at work yet, mm-mm.

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:29.480
Okay then, once the safety device is finished?

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:33.770
Yeah, after I have plenty of data
and make certain it's highly reproducible,

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:36.030
and acknowledge an incontrovertible pathway

00:12:36.030 --> 00:12:38.570
linking to this experiment, mm-hmm.

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.740
How long is that going to take, exactly?!

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:46.330
Well, let's see. At the earliest, a year.
Doing it right, maybe two, mm-hmm.

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:53.210
Hirumi!

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:54.420
Let her go.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.300
But...

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:59.010
I'll admit that two years
seems like a long time.

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:04.390
But Level 6 isn't something
you risk your life attempting to reach.

00:13:04.390 --> 00:13:08.020
Not when, soon enough, the time will
come when anyone can easily attain it,

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:09.270
mm-hmm.

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:24.320
All that's left...

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:28.290
...is to use this special tool to
delete the purchase history, and...

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:30.330
That should about do it.

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:38.250
This is it! It may be Antiskill surplus,
but it was pretty easy to come by.

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:53.520
A promise is a promise, Esther.

00:14:06.160 --> 00:14:11.120
Ahem! Hey there, Esther and Brother!

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:15.620
Recording a special message
like this for you is a bit embarrassing.

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:19.420
So anyway, um, as it happens...

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.300
...I'm dead.

00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:39.690
You should probably have found me by now.
It's a cleaning tank for preservative,

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:44.780
so I doubt I'll be rotting, but I'm pretty
close to naked, which is embarrassing,

00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:48.160
so I'd appreciate it
if you retrieved me right away.

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:51.410
I'm sorry for keeping my medical report
in my bag hidden from you.

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:54.370
It was really hard keeping
the doctor from saying anything,

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:56.540
but it looks like I'm done for.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:56.920
--Hishigata... Hey! Hishigata!

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:59.040
--Getting to Level 6,
--Hishigata... Hey! Hishigata!

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.750
which is beyond even the first-ranked,
who can't even be killed by a nuke...

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:07.930
I thought it would give me
the power of immortality, too, but...

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:12.010
Two years is too far away. Too far away.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:15.680
So now I'm going to turn this into a real race.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:20.730
Brother, Esther, make me a Level 6.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.690
I'm already dead.

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:26.950
At this point, any talk about
safety devices and whatnot won't matter.

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:32.030
So if there's even a 1% chance
of it working then please, do it.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:35.750
I'd appreciate it if my death wasn't in vain.

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:38.920
I'm counting on you, Esther.
And you too, Brother.

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:42.040
Why?! How did this happen?!

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.260
I always kept an eye on Hirumi's vitals.

00:15:44.260 --> 00:15:46.800
If I'd been thinking straight,
I would have realized it.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:49.470
But I deliberately chose to look away...

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:52.220
Hishigata, that's not what's important here.

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:54.810
What's more important than that?!

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:59.270
My little sister... My only other
family has committed suicide!

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:02.060
Yes, but how many minutes
have passed since she died?

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.940
Isn't there anything we can do?

00:16:03.940 --> 00:16:07.740
I promised Hirumi that
if anything happened, I'd help her!

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:09.860
Isn't there anything I can do?!

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:14.790
Let me ask you something first.
Tell me more about your necromancy.

00:16:14.790 --> 00:16:17.620
The Rosenthal techniques place an
outside pseudo-soul into the dead body,

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.540
possessing it and controlling it.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:22.380
It will keep her from decaying, but that's all.

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:27.970
Then it's hopeless. If Hirumi is
no longer Hirumi, it means nothing!

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:29.630
Then...

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:35.640
You said that while the organs were
shut down, the machine would take over.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.770
How about it?

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:40.560
We've never started all body functions
from total shutdown before.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.560
There's no telling what will happen!

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:56.200
Hmm... What's this?
Am I successfully integrated?

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.830
Hirumi!

00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:00.120
Thank goodness...

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:03.750
But this means that everything
has gone the way Hirumi wanted it.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:07.460
Are you sure about that?
Right now, she's just inside the equipment.

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:10.340
I still haven't used any necromancy.

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:15.850
And it was never going to capture
her live soul and put it back to work.

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:18.600
I'll put the ability development mode on freeze.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:21.560
If Hirumi's mind and soul
become diluted and damaged,

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:24.100
then all of this is for nothing.

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:25.860
Hishigata!

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:27.820
What is this? What's going on?

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:31.740
Ah, I've managed to latch on to Hirumi.

00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:33.240
That's incredible!

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:37.240
So, you've finally made up your mind
to do the experiment on Hirumi!

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:38.080
What?

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:41.460
Now the path to Level 6 is right in front of us.

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:45.080
You're an even bigger idiot than I realized.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:48.960
You've fallen behind Esther,
and she didn't even know about carboxylic acid.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:53.510
Hey, come on, what are you talking about?
We all share in success, right?

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:58.930
If it sounds like I'm messing around,
this is your wakeup call!

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:01.100
I will preserve Hirumi's life.

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:04.900
I will by no means be made
your toy and have my life taken!

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:07.110
Hey, what's come over you?

00:18:07.110 --> 00:18:09.980
I'm telling you that I'm taking Hirumi
and we're getting out of here!

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:11.530
I'm exiting this facility--

00:18:11.530 --> 00:18:15.240
no, the very walls of Academy City,
and going into the outside world!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.910
Hishigata, something's wrong!

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:19.240
Oh, no!

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:21.330
Hirumi's heart isn't beating!

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:25.460
Oh, I thought that since Hirumi is dead,
we were working together on her.

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:29.090
No... That can't be. I mean, Hirumi--

00:18:29.090 --> 00:18:33.510
Hi there! Brother,
you just have to get me to Level 6.

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:36.180
Don't turn your eyes down any side paths.

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:38.890
Can you do that for your poor little sister?

00:18:38.890 --> 00:18:39.680
Hirumi?!

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:42.020
Huh? I thought Hirumi was dead.

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:44.100
Don't tell me this is feedback
from the equipment!

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:46.600
You there!

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:50.480
You're emotionally unstable
and not as smart as Brother.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.610
There's only room for one researcher,
so we're done with you.

00:18:56.700 --> 00:19:01.240
If that's your defensive capability,
I don't want you.

00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:07.790
Oh, was that not hard enough?
Well, let me finish the job.

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.000
Stop!

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.130
Huh?

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:14.970
I'm not about to. For a necromancer,
the more corpses the better, right?

00:19:14.970 --> 00:19:17.800
Show us those special pseudo-souls of yours.

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:18.470
What?

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:23.220
If you're not going to help me here,
I may have no more use for you.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:24.770
You couldn't be...

00:19:24.770 --> 00:19:27.190
Hmm? Say it.

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:31.610
I never told Hirumi how I handle bodies,
or about pseudo-souls.

00:19:31.610 --> 00:19:35.990
Which can only mean that
you've taken my control away.

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:39.280
For a secret weapon,
your crisis mentality may be a bit shaky.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:43.080
When you changed your clothes,
did you count your charms?

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:51.420
Qiongqi, Hundun, Taotie...
No, there's one missing!

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:56.340
I was pretty scared to turn my life over
to a technique I'd never seen before.

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:58.840
But if it's a power not even
Brother knows about,

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.640
I thought the outcome
might be different this time.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:06.180
That charm really is amazing.
The moment I touched it, I felt swallowed up,

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:09.440
and the feeling that it was
the real deal gave me tingles.

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:10.400
But that would mean...

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:11.190
Hmm?

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:14.070
You're not Hirumi--

00:20:14.070 --> 00:20:17.740
Ah, that's a pretty big taboo,
so keep it quiet, okay?

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:23.990
It's easier for me to be Hishigata Hirumi
for a while, so I can control Brother.

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:25.540
You're... Taowu...

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:28.460
Don't talk about the person inside me.

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:30.670
Look, we're going to be
with each other for a long while,

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:33.000
so I look forward to working
with you and Brother.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:35.130
Here, for you.

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:38.300
They're for subjects who lose control
from the load of the experiment,

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:42.390
to keep them safely restrained.
You can work those, right?

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:46.100
Or should I use the other
three charms on these other corpses?

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:50.690
Miss Heir of the Rosenthal Style?

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:53.360
Qi--

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:57.940
Gotcha! You realize that's
not going to work, right?

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.110
I can say it outright if you want,
but that's instant death.

00:21:00.110 --> 00:21:02.030
Death in an instant!

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:04.200
Okay, Esther, choose.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:07.330
You can put those cuffs on yourself,
or you can continue resisting.

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:10.910
But every time you fail,
another victim will pay the price.

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:15.290
That coward hiding under
the body of his friend? I'll crush him.

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:17.710
So, what will it be?

00:21:17.710 --> 00:21:21.170
You can't do it, can you?

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:25.390
You can control a corpse,
but it's not the same as returning its soul.

00:21:25.390 --> 00:21:28.520
That's why you can't be
responsible for people's lives.

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:33.020
It's a sad fact, but that's
what it is to be a necromancer.

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:34.400
I'm sorry.

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:36.480
It's okay.

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:38.030
Good.

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:39.860
What are you planning to do now?

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:44.110
Hmm, first thing to do
is to go missing, I suppose.

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.660
But it'll be okay. You still have
your equipment, your subjects,

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:49.950
your researcher, and your necromancer together.

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:53.000
You can pick up your experiments
however you like.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:55.670
Let me give you some hope, Esther.

00:21:55.670 --> 00:22:00.590
Sure, me being alive would be strange.
Taowu's charm is gone, too.

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:04.260
But at what point did the charm even get used?

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:05.510
Was it before I died?

00:22:05.510 --> 00:22:07.720
Or was it after?

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:10.520
Si-xiong talismans can
only be used on dead bodies.

00:22:10.520 --> 00:22:14.770
Which means that if I'm being sustained
by this life support system, I'm alive,

00:22:14.770 --> 00:22:17.940
but if the Si-xiong charm
is controlling me, I'm dead.

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:20.280
So, which one is it?

00:22:20.280 --> 00:22:23.240
It's like Schrödinger's cat, Esther.

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:27.030
Can you tell which one I am right now?

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:30.990
There, you see? You have
a reason to stick with me now.

00:22:33.210 --> 00:22:36.380
So, are you going to help me out?

00:22:36.380 --> 00:22:38.420
Do it for my sake.

00:22:38.420 --> 00:22:40.630
The truth is, I knew.

00:22:40.630 --> 00:22:45.760
That this was nothing more
than a mental leash to make me act.

00:22:45.760 --> 00:22:49.140
That there were no such
self-serving possibilities.

00:22:49.140 --> 00:22:51.470
Still, even so...

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:55.060
I'd appreciate it if my death wasn't in vain.

00:22:55.060 --> 00:22:58.690
I'm counting on you, Esther.
And you too, Brother.

00:22:58.690 --> 00:23:05.030
Even so, it was too painful
to give up... without making sure.

00:23:12.540 --> 00:23:13.950
--Esther!
--Esther!

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:18.380
If I ever need anything,
you can do it for me! Promise, Esther?

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:24.670
Once I use Emperor Shun's Blade, Hirumi will...

00:23:24.670 --> 00:23:26.220
Hirumi will...

00:23:28.090 --> 00:23:30.430
Are you crying, Adonai?

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:34.600
No. Why would I be doing that?
